+## Span omission (D-0189)
+
+A converted file may leave out a whole stretch of its Word original under a
+ruling, declared under `ruled_omissions`:
+
+```yaml
+ruled_omissions:
+  - span:
+      from: "Paragraph text"     # inside the span; omitted: the start
+      from_occurrence: 2         # when the text matches more than once
+      to: "Paragraph text"       # not inside; omitted: the end
+      labels: {first: "o1", last: "o11.2"}   # Word's labels in the span
+    ledger: "D-0189"
+```
+
+Each edge is the whole text of one paragraph at the top level of the Word
+body, whitespace normalised. The `from` paragraph is inside the span, the
+`to` paragraph is not; `from_occurrence` or `to_occurrence` (1-based)
+names one paragraph when the text repeats. The span leaves out everything
+the original holds in it: words, bold, equations, pictures, drawn figures,
+tables and text-box text. The check stops on an edge that matches no
+paragraph, on an edge that matches more than one without an occurrence, on
+edges out of order, on overlapping spans, on a span with no characters, and
+on a span declared for an original that is not Word. The number check
+excuses the run of Word's labels the span names under `labels: {first,
+last}`, and no others. "How this site works" stays true: a span is a listed
+passage.
+
